BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (60% to the buyer's broker and 40% to the seller's broker, so on a $1M commission a broker on a 50/50 house split) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (keeps $300,000 representing the buyer or $200,000 representing the seller [_Shd1I2mefI @ 00:07:06]. David's worked) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (example shows how fast the gross shrinks in practice. A yacht asking $30M sells at $25M for a $1.625M commission,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (but the seller insists on $24M net, which drops the commission to $1M. David defends the 60/40 tilt bluntly, since the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (buyer's broker can always steer the client to another yacht. After the co-broker takes that share, the house keeps) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm ($400,000; a junior broker on 20% walks away with $80,000, while a senior broker on a 50/50 split with no wage clears) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (about $200,000 from the same sale [FpmvbD9-7yc @ 00:13:22]. The lesson in the arithmetic: the headline percentage) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (is never the check.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (Pay structure is where new brokers get burned or protected. The Yacht Broker Masterclass instructor lays out the menu:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (apprentices may get a small basic wage with a lower split, trainee splits run 30/70 or 20/80, the instructor's own first) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (employer paid 20%, and independent contractors get 50/50 but fund their own flights and hotels, the example being) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (trips to the Exumas. The trap is the clawback, where 2,000 to 3,000 a month in pay is treated as an advance against) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (commission and recovered out of the first sale, so it has to be clarified before signing [_Shd1I2mefI @ 00:03:06]. New) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (builds pay differently: Lurssen and Amels deals usually pay about 5% rather than 10%, and Benetti ratchets the fee) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (from introduction only, to introduction plus contract, to full commission for brokers who make regular shipyard visits) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm ([_Shd1I2mefI @ 00:11:20]. David pegs junior house packages at a small wage plus roughly 10 to 20% of the house) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (commission, with office space, cards, boat-show access, and a shared assistant, and notes that a higher wage always) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (means a lower percentage [FpmvbD9-7yc @ 00:07:30]. Charter runs in its own lane: Behind the Gold reports charter) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (brokers earn up to 20%, on superyachts whose running costs sit around 10% of value per year, so a EUR 100M yacht) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (burns roughly EUR 10M annually [LBp3Cz4zFQI @ 00:01:22].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (Aircraft brokerage runs on a tighter cost stack and a sliding fee. Alex Bengoechea prices the toolkit line by line: JetNet) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (at $750 a month on a 12-month contract, Controller ads at $600 to $2,000, and a photographer at $1,500 to $2,000 or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (about $500 for a budget shooter, with the rule to buy subscriptions only when a deal needs them and to start in piston) Tj ET
