BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.00 Tm (Section 4: Firsthand Failure Modes, Traps & Economics Checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 525.77 Tm (The most common way a good deal dies is in the numbers. Charles Weatherly lists the killers as unverifiable) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 510.55 Tm (add-backs, financials that don't tie to tax returns, and owner dependence; once the buyer finds them, the price gets recut) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.32 Tm (in the buyer's favor or the buyer walks, and relistings rarely come back at the same price [55kqfOfgIZw @ 00:00:01].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.10 Tm (Concentration is the trap that can't be patched on deadline: one customer at 38% of revenue can't be fixed "in 60 days") Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 464.87 Tm ([55kqfOfgIZw @ 00:04:32]. Mark Sims watched a $300M-revenue client turn out to be five businesses that had never) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 449.65 Tm (been integrated, so the buyer would not pay full price, and Matt Uhler has seen $300,000 bookkeeper mistakes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.42 Tm ([uG64e1KV1S0 @ 00:13:01]. The economics check cuts deeper than the error itself: an ongoing cost becomes a haircut) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.20 Tm (on value, a one-time cost comes straight off the purchase price, and Uhler reports that buyers often deduct more than) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 403.97 Tm (the fix actually costs. On the presentation side, iGOTHAM warns that hiding weaknesses in the CIM "only creates) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 388.75 Tm (distrust," and Weatherly frames a problem the buyer discovers at week six as broken trust [r1DSXPxZzu8 @ 00:00:48].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 373.52 Tm (The second failure mode is time, and several practitioners price it explicitly. Mark Sims targeted a 3-6 month close,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.30 Tm (saw fatigue set in at 4-6 months, and watched data requests that should take one month stretch to three while the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.07 Tm (buyer's advisor meter kept running [uG64e1KV1S0 @ 00:08:07]; Matt Uhler's rule is "momentum is our friend.") Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 327.85 Tm (Transact Capital builds a 50-plus-page CIP precisely because "time can kill deals," and fewer one-off buyer questions) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 312.62 Tm (means less wasted time [tqw5CWasFOU @ 00:00:27]. Messy paperwork compounds the clock. Mike Zaino's pre-sale) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.40 Tm (cleanup list starts with intellectual property sitting with the founder instead of the company entity, then runs through) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.17 Tm (unpapered ownership promises such as a 5% stake, consents from minority holders and landlords, and lease renewal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 266.95 Tm (rights, all prepared "before engaging with buyers so that we know what we can deliver" [76I0zKp5FM0 @ 00:06:18].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 251.72 Tm (The economics bite on bigger buyers too: Sims notes a PE platform that spends its first year fixing systems is hurting) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 236.50 Tm (its own deal thesis, and bad data shows up as multiple erosion. The Carter Morse & Goodrich seller, who started from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 221.27 Tm (zero, said the process ran harder and longer than expected and would get finances buttoned down before engaging a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.05 Tm (bank next time [a71tQJb9UFE @ 00:01:08].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 190.82 Tm (The third trap is trusting the counterparty before verifying it. Shane Pogue pulled county and assessor records and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 175.60 Tm (ordered mortgage documents on a sponsor's track record and found only one property legitimate; the sponsor had) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 160.37 Tm (hidden a co-GP role, and a "Kansas" apartment was a mirrored image of a Houston building [0Z2XoqRkE00 @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 145.15 Tm (00:11:17]. Pogue's tell for Ponzi schemes tied to real businesses is financial stress, which can usually be spotted) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 129.92 Tm (beforehand, and the fix is continual diligence such as verifying loan volume, built out before it is needed. The OOIDA) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 114.70 Tm (Foundation puts double brokering at an estimated $500-700M in freight a year and tells carriers that a broker never) Tj ET
